# The curated catalog: what deny-unless-allowed admits on its own, the defaults beside the
# model-provider groups in model-provider/. Every line is TLS-inspected and grants `read`, GET and
# HEAD, plus the words written beside it; SECURITY.md, "Reading without being able to write", has
# what each grant opens and what the inspection costs and buys.
#
# Before adding a host, answer all five:
# - why does an arbitrary project need it by default;
# - what sandbox data could be sent to it;
# - does it expose an unauthenticated write endpoint;
# - which grants do its operations call for;
# - could it be project-specific (.ko-agent-sandbox/egress/rule) instead?
# This list stays a small set of intentional data recipients; it never grows by accumulation.

# git repositories: clone and pull are fetch, a POST to .../git-upload-pack, hence git-fetch
allow https://github.com/   read git-fetch
allow https://codeberg.org/ read git-fetch
allow https://gitlab.com/   read git-fetch

